# PHYS 3810 preview lesson index

All five bounded lessons are included. Their availability does not establish
classroom coverage, dates, assessment, delivery responsibility, or required
platforms. The proposed route is three sessions with 50-minute cores and
optional 75-minute expansions; it has not had a human pacing rehearsal.

## Prepare and open the lessons

Use [setup](SETUP.md), then run the root validator before opening the lessons
with the intended Python kernel. Start each notebook from the top. All required
code cells execute during validation even when class discussion uses a subset.

- [Preflight](notebooks/00_setup_preflight.ipynb): versions, a small circuit,
  sampling, and plotting.
- [Grover](notebooks/01_grover.ipynb): phase oracles and amplitude amplification.
  Proposed core: 5 minutes readiness, 10 oracle, 10 diffusion, 20 search and
  sampling, 5 debrief. Expansion adds 15 marked-set and 10 overshooting minutes.
- [QFT](notebooks/02_qft.ipynb) and [QPE](notebooks/03_qpe.ipynb): phase patterns
  and phase estimation. Proposed core: 5 minutes phase/bit order, 15 QFT,
  10 controlled powers, 15 exact phases, 5 decoding. Expansion adds 15 nonexact
  distribution and 10 precision minutes.
- [HHL](notebooks/04_hhl.ipynb) and [compiled Shor](notebooks/05_shor.ipynb):
  restricted applications and resource limits. Proposed core: 5 minutes QPE
  refresher, 20 HHL, 20 Shor, 5 limitations. Expansion adds 15 HHL and 10 Shor
  minutes. The core traces prepared examples, not general algorithm construction.

The two root [statevector](../../notebooks/00_local_statevector_smoke.ipynb) and
[Aer](../../notebooks/01_local_aer_smoke.ipynb) smoke notebooks are also required
by validation; they are setup checks, not additional algorithm lessons.

## Technical references and limits

The [Grover](GROVER_PLAN.md), [QFT](QFT_PLAN.md), [QPE](QPE_PLAN.md),
[HHL](HHL_PLAN.md), and [Shor](SHOR_PLAN.md) references define supported inputs,
bit/register conventions, mathematical acceptance, and costs. They retain
worked expectations, as do the notebooks and tests. This preview does not
provide a concealed-answer assessment.

Separate instructor guides and presenter answer documents are not included.
Follow eventual instructor directions about solutions and submitted work.
See [validation and platform limits](../../VALIDATION.md) for the current
160-test/eight-notebook inventory and the distinction between code execution
and classroom readiness.
